### AGROLINK API TESTS
# You can run these tests using the "REST Client" extension in VS Code.
# Just click the "Send Request" button above any of the requests below.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api

### 1. Register a Farmer
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "farmer_kamal@email.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "role": "FARMER",
    "nic": "901234567V"
}


### 2. Register an Admin (For Testing Approvals)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "admin_sunil@email.com",
    "password": "adminpass",
    "role": "ADMIN"
}


### 3. Login as Farmer (Copy the 'userId' from the response!)
# @name farmerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "farmer_kamal@email.com",
    "password": "password123"
}


### 4. Create a Farmer Project
# Note: In a real flow, you'd extract the Farmer's ID from the login.
# For now, replace "FARMER_ID_HERE" with the ID you got from Login!
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "farmerId": "FARMER_ID_HERE",
    "projectName": "Maha Season Rice - 2026",
    "location": "Anuradhapura",
    "cropType": "Rice",
    "expectedYield": "1500kg",
    "startDate": "2026-03-01",
    "mediaUrls": ["https://example.com/field_image.jpg"]
}


### 5. Admin View Pending Projects (Copy the 'id' of the project created above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/pending


### 6. Admin Approve the Project
# Replace "PROJECT_ID_HERE" with the ID of the Pending Project!
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/PROJECT_ID_HERE/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "totalFundingGoal": 250000,
    "minimumFundingToStart": 100000,
    "minimumInvestmentPerInvestor": 5000,
    "verifiedExpectedYield": "1450kg",
    "estimatedIncome": "300000"
}


### 7. View All Approved Projects (What Investors See)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/approved


### 8. Invest in a Project
# Replace the IDs below!
POST {{baseUrl}}/investments/invest
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "projectId": "PROJECT_ID_HERE",
    "investorId": "INVESTOR_ID_HERE",
    "amount": 50000
}
